Package: netLOO
Title: Leave-One-Out Contribution Analysis for Multi-Temporal Bipartite Networks
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Francisco E.", "Fontúrbel", , "francisco.fonturbel@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Rodrigo", "Medel", role = "aut"))
Description: A dataset-agnostic toolkit for multi-temporal bipartite
    network analysis (e.g. plant-pollinator webs sampled across years or
    conditions). Computes per-network structural metrics, species
    persistence and turnover, pairwise interaction beta diversity, null
    models, rarefaction, and a leave-one-out contribution analysis that
    quantifies how much each time point uniquely contributes to the
    pooled metaweb, relative to what would be expected. Generalizes the
    analysis pipeline from Medel & Fontúrbel's blooming-desert
    plant-pollinator study to any set of bipartite networks sampled at
    three or more time points.
